  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Late-inning rallies have become the Padres' signature. This time it held.",
    "what_this_means": "Trailing 1\u20130 through eight innings, the Padres needed Michael King to be exceptional and they got exactly that: 5.2 innings, one earned run, five strikeouts. The offense was a problem until it wasn't. They had almost nothing until Sheets lifted one over the fence in the ninth, turning a deficit into a 3\u20131 win. King's start bought them the time to find that moment. Estrada, Adam, and Miller closed the gap after he left, giving the lineup a live 9th inning to work with. Sheets didn't waste it. This is how thin margins get held: pitching gives you air, and one swing makes it count. They won by one run again. That math gets harder every time.",
    "what_to_watch": "Kyle Harrison carries a 2.41 ERA into tonight's rematch at American Family Field. The Padres' lineup struck out 13 times yesterday. Griffin Canning will need the same margin King got.",
